From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 16:30:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: Add the NPU

The A733 has a Vivante NPU, which the etnaviv driver binds through the
generic "vivante,gc" compatible, as on the A523.

- reg: the NPU window of the memory map, 0x03600000-0x03600fff.
- interrupts: INTID 97, the NPU's only interrupt line.
- clocks: "bus" is the MBUS gate of the NPU, the master interface to
  memory. "core" is the NPU module clock, which runs from PLL_NPU out of
  reset. "reg" is the NPU gate of its bus gating reset register; its
  parent is the AHB matrix gate of the NPU.
- resets: core, AXI, AHB and SRAM, in the order of the binding.
- power-domains: PD_NPU of the PCK-600.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; etnaviv binds the NPU
with its clocks, resets and power domain, the module clock runs from
PLL_NPU, and the "bus" and "reg" gates are off in runtime suspend. No
job was submitted.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
index e4cc492a5565..d5c181e8b056 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
@@ -794,6 +794,18 @@ ppi_partition1: interrupt-partition-1 {
 			};
 		};
 
+		npu: npu@3600000 {
+			compatible = "vivante,gc";
+			reg = <0x03600000 0x1000>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 65 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>;
+			clocks = <&ccu CLK_MBUS_NPU>, <&ccu CLK_NPU>,
+				 <&ccu CLK_BUS_NPU>;
+			clock-names = "bus", "core", "reg";
+			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_NPU_CORE>, <&ccu RST_BUS_NPU_AXI>,
+				 <&ccu RST_BUS_NPU_AHB>, <&ccu RST_BUS_NPU_SRAM>;
+			power-domains = <&pck600 PD_NPU>;
+		};
+
 		iommu0: iommu@3900000 {
 			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-iommu";
 			reg = <0x03900000 0x10000>;
